<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:base="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl">
  <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl">
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-assets.owl"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-vocab.owl"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/cti/stix/observed-data"/>
    <rdfs:label>grid_stix_2_1_declarations</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Domain-agnostic declared-value and discrepancy-comparison extensions for Grid-STIX 2.1. Positioned in core (not a domain-specific module) because comparing a self-reported/declared value against independently observed evidence is not specific to any one domain — it applies equally to a nuclear facility's declared operational status, a grid asset's declared firmware version or compliance certification, or any other self-attested state checked against observed reality.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Ontology>

  <!-- =============================================== -->
  <!-- DECLARATION -->
  <!-- =============================================== -->

  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration">
    <rdfs:comment>A self-reported or declared value about an entity, asserted by some source, without independent verification. No specific STIX object type represents this well, so it is a new root concept rather than a forced subclass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declaration</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declared-entity-ref">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-assets.owl#physical-asset"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the entity the declaration is about.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declared_entity_ref</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declared-value">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The self-reported value being declared.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declared_value</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration-source">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Who or what asserted this declared value (e.g., a regulatory database, vendor self-attestation).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declaration_source</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declared-as-of">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>When the declared value was asserted to hold.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declared_as_of</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <!-- =============================================== -->
  <!-- DISCREPANCY -->
  <!-- =============================================== -->

  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/cti/stix/observed-data"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The typed outcome of comparing a Declaration against independently observed evidence: agreement, contradiction, or a lead/lag in timing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>discrepancy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#compares-declaration">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declaration"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the Declaration this discrepancy evaluates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>compares_declaration</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#compares-evidence">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/cti/stix/observed-data"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the independently observed evidence compared against the declaration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>compares_evidence</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy-type">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-vocab.owl#discrepancy_type_ov"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Type of disagreement between the declared value and the observed evidence, from a controlled vocabulary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>discrepancy_type</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#declared-state">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Snapshot of the declared state at comparison time. Named to parallel previous-state/new-state in the events-observables module.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>declared_state</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#implied-state">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Snapshot of the state implied by the observed evidence at comparison time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>implied_state</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#confidence">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Confidence that this discrepancy is real and actionable, 0-100 inclusive. Locally declared (not inherited from cti:confidence) for reliable code generation, but deliberately mirrors cti:confidence's 0-100 integer convention for consistency with core STIX semantics. A simple range is used deliberately: this generator's range parser does not resolve complex restricted-datatype expressions (confirmed empirically), unlike the simple XSD-type references used throughout this codebase.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>confidence</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#compares-events">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#discrepancy"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Per-event breakdown of the evidence this discrepancy aggregates. Additive alongside compares-evidence (which points at the underlying raw ObservedData): a discrepancy's declared-state/implied-state is the aggregate outcome across potentially several distinct lifecycle-event signals, each independently typed and scored.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>compares_events</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <!-- =============================================== -->
  <!-- LIFECYCLE EVENT -->
  <!-- =============================================== -->

  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event">
    <rdfs:comment>A typed transition signal extracted from a single piece of independently observed evidence, comparable against a Declaration. Domain-agnostic, like declaration/discrepancy: the same shape (a dated, typed, evidence-bound claim about a state transition) applies beyond reactor lifecycle status.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>lifecycle-event</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#event-entity-ref">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-assets.owl#physical-asset"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the entity this event is about. Mirrors declared-entity-ref.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>event_entity_ref</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#event-type">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-vocab.owl#lifecycle_event_type_ov"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Type of lifecycle transition this event describes, from a controlled vocabulary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>event_type</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#event-implied-state">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The state this specific event implies. A separate property from discrepancy's implied-state (not a shared domain) since an instance cannot be both a discrepancy and a lifecycle-event.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>event_implied_state</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#event-evidence-ref">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/cti/stix/observed-data"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the independently observed evidence (real STIX ObservedData) this event was extracted from.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>event_evidence_ref</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#plant-match-score">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Confidence, 0.0-1.0, that this event's evidence was correctly bound to the declared entity (as opposed to a same-named or unrelated one).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>plant_match_score</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#unit-bound">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.anl.gov/sss/grid-stix-2.1-declarations.owl#lifecycle-event"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
    <rdfs:comment>True when the evidence text bound this event to a specific sub-unit of the entity, not just the entity as a whole.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>unit_bound</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>

</rdf:RDF>
